# Guitar MP3 Transcription\n\nA full-stack local web app for uploading a guitar MP3 and generating a PDF guitar score/tab.\n\n## What this app does\n\n- Accepts an MP3 upload from a browser UI\n- Runs polyphonic transcription using Spotify Basic Pitch\n- Groups simultaneous notes into chord-like events\n- Maps detected pitches onto plausible guitar fretboard positions\n- Exports:\n  - a PDF guitar score/tab summary\n  - a JSON transcription artifact\n\n## Project structure\n\n- `frontend/index.html` — browser UI\n- `backend/app/main.py` — FastAPI server\n- `backend/app/transcription.py` — transcription pipeline\n- `backend/app/guitar.py` — guitar tuning and fretboard mapping helpers\n- `backend/app/pdf_render.py` — PDF rendering\n- `backend/uploads/` — uploaded MP3 files\n- `backend/outputs/` — generated PDFs and JSON files\n\n## Important limitations\n\nThis is a practical prototype, not a studio-grade transcription engine.\n\n- `Basic Pitch` is strong for polyphonic note estimation, but it does not inherently understand guitar fingering.\n- The chord detection here is inferred by grouping note onsets, not by semantic harmonic analysis.\n- The generated PDF is a simplified guitar score/tab layout, not full engraved notation like MuseScore/LilyPond output.\n- Dense mixes or non-isolated guitar audio will reduce quality.\n\n## Backend setup\n\nFrom `backend/`:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n```\n\nServer runs at:\n\n- `http://127.0.0.1:8000`\n\n## Frontend setup\n\nServe the frontend folder with any static server. For example:\n\n```bash\ncd frontend\npython3 -m http.server 3000\n```\n\nOpen:\n\n- `http://127.0.0.1:3000`\n\n## API\n\n### `GET /api/health`\nReturns API health status.\n\n### `POST /api/transcribe`\nForm fields:\n- `file`: MP3 file\n- `tuning`: `standard` | `drop-d` | `dadgad` | `open-g`\n- `detail`: `fast` | `balanced` | `deep`\n- `filename`: output PDF filename\n\nReturns JSON with:\n- `pdf_url`\n- `json_url`\n- note and chord counts\n- warnings\n\n## Recommended future improvements\n\n- Use source separation before transcription to isolate guitar\n- Add beat/bar quantization for cleaner notation\n- Export MusicXML instead of direct PDF drawing\n- Render via LilyPond or MuseScore for professional engraving\n- Improve chord naming and voicing heuristics\n- Add support for bends, slides, hammer-ons, pull-offs, and rhythmic notation\n